  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**  \n   We use a hierarchical optimization algorithm that combines multi-resolution analysis with adaptive gradient-based methods. The approach addresses the problem's non-convex nature by:\n   - **Resolution Adaptation**: Starting from a coarse grid (70 points) and iteratively refining to higher resolutions (140, 280, 500) allows exploration of simple and complex morphologies while preserving integral constraints via muting.\n   - **Gradient Balancing**: Contrasts between orthogonal low-frequency and high-frequency components are biased toward distinct lags to selectively penalize overlaps.\n   - **Sparse Projection**: Adaptive projection focuses computation on the most influential components, reducing gradient approximation costs.\n   - **Free Nullspace Evaluation**: Derive low-frequency bases for accelerated convergence.\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**  \n   Variables:  \n   - \\( h \\in \\mathbb{R}^N \\), \\(N \\in \\{70,140,280,500\\} \\)\n   - \\( \\Delta x = 2/N \\)\n   - Objective: \\( C_5 = \\max_k \\Delta x \\cdot \\sum_{i} h_i(1 - h_{i+k}) \\) (finite difference approximation)\n\n   Constraints:  \n   - \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\)\n   - \\( \\sum_i h_i \\cdot \\Delta x = 1 \\)\n\n   Decomposition:  \n   - Projected Gradient: Minimizes \\( C_5 \\) iteratively with \\( g_k^{(t)} = \\hat{H} \\ln(\\lambda_k^{(t)}) - \\xi_k^{(t)} \\)  \n   - Joint Optimization: With \\( \\zeta \\)-regularized budget balancing  \n   - Component Separation: Low-pass \\( \\approx \\int h \\,dx = 1 \\), High-pass \\( \\approx \\sum h^2 = N \\)\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**  \n   **Phase A: Initialization**  \n   - Input: `seed`, `budget_s`, `initial_h_values` (n=280 if available)\n   - Construct initial candidates via:  \n     - **Uniform Shuffling**: \\( h = [1/2 \\text{ if randomly flipped}, 0 \\text{ otherwise}] \\) with \\( \\sum = N/2 \\)\n     - **Orthogonal Projection**: \\( h = \\text{project\\_phase}(\\text{random}, \\phi=0.7) \\)\n\n   **Phase B: Multi-Resolution Optimization**  \n   - Resolution cycles: `resolutions = [min(140, len(initial_h_values)), 280, 500]`\n   - For each `N` in `resolutions` (if \\( N \\neq \\) current length):  \n     - Interpolate `h` from \\(N_{\\text{prev}}\\) to `N`  \n     - Initialize with \\( H_0 = \\text{random\\_validation}() \\) (if `initial_h_values` exists)  \n     - Allocate budget: \\( \\text{time}_{N} = \\min(\\text{budget}_{\\text{remaining}}, 100 + N/10) \\)  \n     - Optimize with projected gradient:  \n       - Objective: \\( \\min C_5 \\) via \\( \\text{soft\\_max}\\left(\\sum_{k} \\varphi_k \\cdot \\exp(-\\lambda_k C_5^{(k)})\\right) \\)  \n       - Gradient: \\( g = \\nabla C_5 - \\alpha \\cdot \\nabla(\\sum h_i \\Delta x) \\) with \\( \\alpha = \\text{AdaGrad}(t) \\)  \n   - Adjust proxy penalty \\( \\phi = 0.1 \\cdot \\) number of levels\n\n   **Phase C: Convergence**  \n   - Terminate if:  \n     - Time elapsed \\( \\geq \\text{budget\\_s} - 30 \\)  \n     - Target \\( C_5^{(N)} \\) plateau across \\( \\geq 5 \\) iterations  \n   - Compare candidates: Return minimal \\( C_5 \\) solution across all resolutions.\n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**  \n   - **Resolution Levels**: `resolutions = [min(140, len(initial_h_values)), 280, 500]`  \n   - **Penalty Balance**: \\( \\varrho = 0.1, 0.3, 0.6 \\) for low/high window focus  \n   - **Dithering**: Add Gaussian noise \\( \\epsilon \\sim (0, 0.1/ \\sqrt{N}) \\) during projection  \n   - **Fallback**: If `initial_h_values` exists and no improvement, use multscale projection \\( h \\leftarrow \\text{project\\_phase}(h, \\phi) \\)\n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**  \n   - Resolution \\(N\\) inversion: \\( O(N^2) \\) for correlation + \\( O(N) \\) projection  \n   - Parallelsim: 1 CPU \u2192 Allocate \\( t_{\\text{max}} = \\text{budget\\_s}/3 \\) per resolution  \n   - Early exit: Compute fallback after each level \\(N\\) if integral \\( \\neq 1 \\) within \\( \\epsilon = 1e-5 \\)  \n   - N-level fallback: Use spline projection \\( \\approx \\Delta x \\cdot \\text{B-spline}(h, N) \\)\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**  \n   - Candidate criteria:  \n     - \\( 0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1 \\) for all \\( i, N \\)  \n     - \\( \\left| \\sum_i h_i \\cdot \\Delta x - 1 \\right| < 1e-4 \\)  \n     - \\( C_5_{\\text{computed}} < \\text{previous} \\)  \n   - Output: \\( (h_{\\text{best}}, C_5_{\\text{best}}, N_{\\text{best}}) \\)  \n   - Evaluator: Use `np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\") * \\Delta x` and clip na\u00efve\\non-negative\n   \n   **Expert engineering note**:  \n   Avoid dense-gradient computations by Taylor-approximating \\( \\sum_{k} \\varphi_k \\) at critical lags.  \n   Use Ortho-Project (\u7fa9\u52d9 sp \\text{sign}\\cdot\\text{Tikz}) for faster convergence.",
